course: dictionary
lesson: 14774
title: Where things come from
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Provenance is a long, formal word, but the idea is simple: it tells you where something comes from. Its origin is its starting point. «The museum label shows the provenance of every vase in the hall.» The label tells you where each vase came from.
explain: Provenance can also mean the story of an object's owners. «The painting's provenance shows it hung in a palace, then in a family home.» A clear provenance helps experts prove that an object is real and was not stolen.
explain: Shops use the word too. «The sign gives the provenance of the apples: they were grown in a Kent orchard.» Here provenance means the place the food came from. To check a meaning, swap in "where it comes from" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Provenance means where something comes from, or its origin.
fact: Provenance can also mean the record of where an object has been and who has owned it.
fact: Provenance is a formal word, so you will often meet it in museums, history books and food labels.
fact: «Origin» is a close synonym for provenance, but provenance often includes the story of an object's past owners.
fact: In history and museums, a clear provenance helps prove an object is real and was not stolen.
exercise: «The shop label told us the provenance of the cheese.» What does provenance mean here? | How the cheese tastes | The price of the cheese | The shape of the box | *Where the cheese came from
exercise: «The painting's provenance showed it had once hung in a palace.» What does provenance tell us about the painting? | Its colours only | Its size and frame | How much it weighs | *Its history of where it has been and who owned it
exercise: «The museum wants to know the provenance of the ancient vase.» Find and copy the word that means where something comes from. | ancient | museum | *provenance | vase
test: «A clear provenance helps experts prove an object is real.» What does provenance mean in this sentence? | The day the object was made | *The history of where the object has been and who owned it | The size of the object | A kind of paint
test: «Shops label the provenance of meat and fruit so you know where it was grown or raised.» Which words are closest in meaning to provenance here? | How long the food lasts | *Where the food came from | Who cooked the food | How much the food costs
exam: Which best explains what provenance means? | A type of cloud that brings rain | A way of cooking eggs | *A record of where something came from and who owned it | The sound a bell makes
